WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.850
A mushroom pushes up
out of the ground.

2
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.470
It stays in one place.

3
00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:07.890
It can't walk, and it
looks a lot like a plant.

4
00:00:07.940 --> 00:00:10.470
Many people would file it with
the plants without a second

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:11.550
thought.

6
00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.310
Yet biologists don't count a
mushroom as a plant at all.

7
00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:16.510
Why not?

8
00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.970
In this mission, you'll see how
biologists sort living things

9
00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.400
into groups by the
features they share.

10
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:25.470
You'll compare the features that
set the big groups of living

11
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:26.690
things apart.

12
00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:29.830
And you'll practise using those
features to place an organism

13
00:00:29.880 --> 00:00:31.750
in the right group.

14
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:36.010
Your mission: find out why
a mushroom isn't a plant.
